`s 12(6): the income of a person for the base calendar year for the month` month facts MEANS
    `the income of a person for a calendar year` month facts

§ `Additional amount, section 12.1`

-- 12.1: from the payment quarter beginning on July 1, 2011 an amount "that may be added to the amount of the
-- supplement that may be paid under section 12" is determined by the formula A x B - C/4, with A a fixed sum that is
-- indexed from quarter to quarter, B the pensioner's special qualifying factor for the month and C a reduction
-- worked out from the income for the base calendar year. Subsection (1) is for a pensioner referred to in paragraph
-- 12(1)(a), subsection (2) for one referred to in paragraph 12(1)(b).

-- A for the payment quarter beginning on July 1, 2011: (1) $50; (2)(a) $50 for a pensioner referred to in
-- subparagraph 12(1)(b)(i); (2)(b) $35 for one referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(b)(ii).
-- src:331 | A is $50;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 12.1(1) "A is $50" (src:331)
-- src:340 | A is
-- src:341 | (a) in the case of a pensioner referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(b)(i), $50, and
-- src:342 | (b) in the case of a pensioner referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(b)(ii), $35;
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 12.1(2) A (src:340-342)
GIVEN situation IS A `s 12(1): Situation of the pensioner`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 12.1: the amount determined for A for the payment quarter beginning on July 1, 2011` situation MEANS
    CONSIDER situation
    WHEN `s 12(1)(a): a person other than a person described in paragraph (b)` THEN 50
    WHEN `s 12(1)(b)(i): a person whose spouse or common-law partner has no pension payable yet in the quarter` THEN 50
    WHEN `s 12(1)(b)(ii): a person whose spouse or common-law partner has a pension payable from this month` THEN 35

-- (1) C is
-- (a) in the case of a pensioner who has no spouse or common-law partner, 1/12 of the pensioner's income for the base
--     calendar year in excess of $2,000 rounded, if it is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of
--     four dollars, and
-- (b) in the case of a pensioner who, on the day immediately before the current payment period, had a spouse or
--     common-law partner to whom no benefit may be paid for any month in the current payment period, 1/24 of the
--     aggregate of the income of the pensioner and his or her spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year
--     in excess of $4,000 rounded, if it is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of four dollars.
-- The rounding is read as applying to the monthly figure that results (fork F-12.1-1); an income not in excess of the
-- sum gives nothing. A pensioner with a spouse or common-law partner to whom a benefit (an allowance, for example) may
-- be paid is in neither (a) nor (b): the Act gives no C, so the answer is NOTHING (fork F-12.1-2).
-- src:328 | 12.1 (1) The amount that may be added to the amount of the supplement that may be paid under section 12 to a pensioner referred to in paragraph 12(1)(a) for any month in a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011 is the amount determined by the formula
-- src:329 | A × B – C/4
-- src:330 | where
-- src:331 | A is $50;
-- src:332 | B is the pensioner’s special qualifying factor for the month; and
-- src:333 | C is
-- src:334 | (a) in the case of a pensioner who has no spouse or common-law partner, 1/12 of the pensioner’s income for the base calendar year in excess of $2,000 rounded, if it is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of four dollars, and
-- src:335 | (b) in the case of a pensioner who, on the day immediately before the current payment period, had a spouse or common-law partner to whom no benefit may be paid for any month in the current payment period, 1/24 of the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and his or her spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year in excess of $4,000 rounded, if it is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of four dollars.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 12.1(1) (src:328-335)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the amount determined for A` IS A NUMBER
      `the pensioner's special qualification facts` IS A `Special qualification facts`
      `the pensioner has no spouse or common-law partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on the day immediately before the current payment period the pensioner had a spouse or common-law partner to whom no benefit may be paid for any month in the current payment period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income of the pensioner for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 12.1(1): the amount determined by the formula for a pensioner referred to in paragraph 12(1)(a)` month `the amount determined for A` `the pensioner's special qualification facts` `the pensioner has no spouse or common-law partner` `on the day immediately before the current payment period the pensioner had a spouse or common-law partner to whom no benefit may be paid for any month in the current payment period` `the income of the pensioner for the base calendar year` `the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the pensioner has no spouse or common-law partner`
        THEN JUST ((`the amount determined for A` TIMES factorB) MINUS (cNoSpouse DIVIDED BY 4))
        IF `on the day immediately before the current payment period the pensioner had a spouse or common-law partner to whom no benefit may be paid for any month in the current payment period`
        THEN JUST ((`the amount determined for A` TIMES factorB) MINUS (cSpouse DIVIDED BY 4))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        factorB MEANS `the special qualifying factor of a person for the month containing` month `the pensioner's special qualification facts`
        cNoSpouse MEANS ((max 0 (`the income of the pensioner for the base calendar year` MINUS 2000)) DIVIDED BY 12) `rounded to the next lower multiple of` 4
        cSpouse MEANS ((max 0 (`the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` MINUS 4000)) DIVIDED BY 24) `rounded to the next lower multiple of` 4

-- (2) C is 1/24 of the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and his or her spouse or common-law partner for the
-- base calendar year in excess of $4,000 rounded, if it is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple
-- of four dollars.
-- src:337 | (2) The amount that may be added to the amount of the supplement that may be paid under section 12 to a pensioner referred to in paragraph 12(1)(b) for any month in a payment quarter beginning after June 30, 2011 is the amount determined by the formula
-- src:338 | A × B – C/4
-- src:339 | where
-- src:340 | A is
-- src:341 | (a) in the case of a pensioner referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(b)(i), $50, and
-- src:342 | (b) in the case of a pensioner referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(b)(ii), $35;
-- src:343 | B is the pensioner’s special qualifying factor for the month; and
-- src:344 | C is 1/24 of the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and his or her spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year in excess of $4,000 rounded, if it is not a multiple of four dollars, to the next lower multiple of four dollars.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 12.1(2) (src:337-344)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the amount determined for A` IS A NUMBER
      `the pensioner's special qualification facts` IS A `Special qualification facts`
      `the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 12.1(2): the amount determined by the formula for a pensioner referred to in paragraph 12(1)(b)` month `the amount determined for A` `the pensioner's special qualification facts` `the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` MEANS
    (`the amount determined for A` TIMES factorB) MINUS (cReduction DIVIDED BY 4)
    WHERE
        factorB MEANS `the special qualifying factor of a person for the month containing` month `the pensioner's special qualification facts`
        cReduction MEANS ((max 0 (`the aggregate of the income of the pensioner and the spouse or common-law partner for the base calendar year` MINUS 4000)) DIVIDED BY 24) `rounded to the next lower multiple of` 4

-- The amount "that may be added" is not a negative sum: where the formula comes out below nothing, nothing is added
-- (fork F-12-2, as for section 12(5)).
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 12.1(1), s 12.1(2) (src:328-344)
GIVEN formula IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 12.1: the amount that may be added, given the amount determined by the formula` formula MEANS
    CONSIDER formula
    WHEN JUST amount THEN JUST (max 0 amount)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- (2.1) For any month in the payment quarter beginning on July 1, 2016, (a) A in subsection (1), and (b) A in
-- subsection (2) in the case set out in paragraph (a) of A in that subsection, is the amount that would otherwise
-- have been determined plus $78.92. So the increase is for a pensioner of paragraph 12(1)(a) or of subparagraph
-- 12(1)(b)(i); not for one of subparagraph 12(1)(b)(ii).
-- src:346 | (2.1) For any month in the payment quarter beginning on July 1, 2016,
-- src:347 | (a) the amount determined for A in subsection (1) is the amount that would otherwise have been determined for A in that subsection for any month in that payment quarter plus $78.92; and
-- src:348 | (b) the amount determined for A in subsection (2) in the case set out in paragraph (a) of A in that subsection is the amount that would otherwise have been determined in that case for A in that subsection for any month in that payment quarter plus $78.92.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 12.1(2.1) (src:346-348)
GIVEN situation IS A `s 12(1): Situation of the pensioner`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 12.1(2.1): the increase for the payment quarter beginning on July 1, 2016` situation MEANS
    CONSIDER situation
    WHEN `s 12(1)(a): a person other than a person described in paragraph (b)` THEN 78.92
    WHEN `s 12(1)(b)(i): a person whose spouse or common-law partner has no pension payable yet in the quarter` THEN 78.92
    WHEN `s 12(1)(b)(ii): a person whose spouse or common-law partner has a pension payable from this month` THEN 0

-- (3), (4), (5) and (2.1) together: for a payment quarter beginning after September 30, 2011 the amount determined
-- for A is the amount for the three-month period immediately before multiplied by the ratio of the first adjustment
-- quarter's index to the second's (3); never less than that amount (4); and with no adjustment after a fall in the
-- index until the index recovers, the earlier second index then being deemed the second index (5). For the quarter
-- beginning on July 1, 2016 the increase of (2.1) is added. A quarter that does not begin after September 30, 2011
-- is not covered: NOTHING.
-- src:349 | Indexation
-- src:350 | (3) Subject to subsection (2.1), for the purpose of calculating the amount payable under subsection (1) or (2) for any month in a payment quarter beginning after September 30, 2011, the amount to be determined for A in that subsection is the amount obtained by multiplying
-- src:351 | (a) the amount determined for A for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter
-- src:352 | by
-- src:353 | (b) the ratio that the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter bears to the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to that payment quarter.
-- src:354 | No decrease
-- src:355 | (4) Despite subsection (3), the amount determined for A for any month in a payment quarter shall not be less than the amount determined for A for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter.
-- src:356 | Effect of reduction in Consumer Price Index
-- src:357 | (5) If, in relation to any payment quarter, the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter is lower than the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter,
-- src:358 | (a) no adjustment to the amount determined for A shall be made under subsection (3) in respect of that payment quarter; and
-- src:359 | (b) no adjustment to the amount determined for A shall be made under subsection (3) in respect of any subsequent payment quarter until, in relation to a subsequent payment quarter, the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to that subsequent payment quarter is higher than the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter referred to in paragraph (a), in which case the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter referred to in that paragraph is deemed to be the second adjustment quarter that relates to that subsequent payment quarter.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 12.1(2.1), s 12.1(3), s 12.1(4), s 12.1(5) (src:346-359)
GIVEN `the first day of the payment quarter` IS A DATE
      situation IS A `s 12(1): Situation of the pensioner`
      `the amount determined for A for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` IS A NUMBER
      `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `oa2 indexation: Outcome of a payment quarter`
`s 12.1(3): the amount determined for A for a payment quarter beginning after September 30, 2011` `the first day of the payment quarter` situation `the amount determined for A for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter` `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply` MEANS
    IF `the first day of the payment quarter` AT MOST (YearMonthDay 2011 9 30)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`oa2 indexation: Outcome of a payment quarter` WITH
                   `the amount for the payment quarter` IS indexed's `the amount for the payment quarter` PLUS fixedIncrease
                   `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply` IS indexed's `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply`)
    WHERE
        indexed MEANS
            `oa2 indexation: the outcome for a payment quarter`
                `the amount determined for A for any month in the three-month period immediately before that payment quarter`
                `the Consumer Price Index for the first adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter`
                `the Consumer Price Index for the second adjustment quarter that relates to the payment quarter`
                `the Consumer Price Index of the earlier second adjustment quarter still deemed to apply`
        fixedIncrease MEANS
            IF `the first day of the payment quarter` EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2016 7 1)
            THEN `s 12.1(2.1): the increase for the payment quarter beginning on July 1, 2016` situation
            ELSE 0
